-80\% and 77\% (Figure~\ref{fig:reliability}, Appendix~\ref{app:figs}); this is the family's pre-named calibration comparison and
-\textbf{the only one that survives Holm correction on both benchmark versions} (Table~\ref{tab:holm}). The
-dense-similarity signal is already nearly calibrated, and its reduction is not significant ($p=0.27$ and
-$0.10$). Platt scaling and histogram binning, fit on the same folds, reduce ECE by similar amounts, with
-overlapping bootstrap intervals; histogram binning's lowest ECE partly reflects being scored on the bins it
